  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Factorise each of the following expressions:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$3(x+2)^2+4(x+2)+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+3)(3x+7)$\n\nLet $y=x+2$ and factorise the quadratic in $y$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x+2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3y^2+4y+1&=3y^2+3y+y+1\\\\3y^2+4y+1&=3y(y+1)+(y+1)\\\\3y^2+4y+1&=(3y+1)(y+1)\\\\3(x+2)^2+4(x+2)+1&=[3(x+2)+1][(x+2)+1]\\\\3(x+2)^2+4(x+2)+1&=(3x+7)(x+3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$6(x+1)^2+7(x+1)+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2x+3)(3x+5)$\n\nLet $y=x+1$ and factorise the quadratic in $y$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6y^2+7y+2&=6y^2+3y+4y+2\\\\6y^2+7y+2&=3y(2y+1)+2(2y+1)\\\\6y^2+7y+2&=(3y+2)(2y+1)\\\\6(x+1)^2+7(x+1)+2&=[3(x+1)+2][2(x+1)+1]\\\\6(x+1)^2+7(x+1)+2&=(3x+5)(2x+3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2(x-1)^2-(x-1)-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(2x-5)$\n\nLet $y=x-1$ and factorise the quadratic in $y$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2y^2-y-3&=2y^2+2y-3y-3\\\\2y^2-y-3&=2y(y+1)-3(y+1)\\\\2y^2-y-3&=(2y-3)(y+1)\\\\2(x-1)^2-(x-1)-3&=[2(x-1)-3][(x-1)+1]\\\\2(x-1)^2-(x-1)-3&=x(2x-5)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$3(x-2)^2-16(x-2)+5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-7)(3x-7)$\n\nLet $y=x-2$ and factorise the quadratic in $y$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x-2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3y^2-16y+5&=3y^2-15y-y+5\\\\3y^2-16y+5&=3y(y-5)-(y-5)\\\\3y^2-16y+5&=(3y-1)(y-5)\\\\3(x-2)^2-16(x-2)+5&=[3(x-2)-1][(x-2)-5]\\\\3(x-2)^2-16(x-2)+5&=(3x-7)(x-7)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$16(x+3)^2+16(x+3)+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(4x+13)(4x+15)$\n\nLet $y=x+3$ and factorise the quadratic in $y$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x+3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}16y^2+16y+3&=16y^2+4y+12y+3\\\\16y^2+16y+3&=4y(4y+1)+3(4y+1)\\\\16y^2+16y+3&=(4y+3)(4y+1)\\\\16(x+3)^2+16(x+3)+3&=[4(x+3)+3][4(x+3)+1]\\\\16(x+3)^2+16(x+3)+3&=(4x+15)(4x+13)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$6(2x-1)^2-5(2x-1)-6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(6x-1)(4x-5)$\n\nLet $y=2x-1$ and factorise the quadratic in $y$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=2x-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6y^2-5y-6&=6y^2+4y-9y-6\\\\6y^2-5y-6&=2y(3y+2)-3(3y+2)\\\\6y^2-5y-6&=(2y-3)(3y+2)\\\\6(2x-1)^2-5(2x-1)-6&=[2(2x-1)-3][3(2x-1)+2]\\\\6(2x-1)^2-5(2x-1)-6&=(4x-5)(6x-1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
